# Question 02 : 
    Using CSS Grid, create a 2x2 grid layout where the first row spans two
    columns, and the second row has two equal columns. Provide the HTML and CSS code
    snippets.

# Answer 02 : 
    To create a 2×2 grid layout, we use CSS Grid.
    In this layout:

    The first row spans two columns.

    The second row contains two equal columns.

    HTML Code : 
        <div class="grid-container">
            <div class="item1">Header</div>
            <div class="item2">Box 1</div>
            <div class="item3">Box 2</div>
        </div>


    CSS Code :
        .grid-container {
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
            gap: 10px;
        }

        .item1 {
            grid-column: 1 / 3;
            background-color: lightblue;
            padding: 20px;
            text-align: center;
        }

        .item2, .item3 {
            background-color: lightgray;
            padding: 20px;
            text-align: center;
        }


