# Question 08 : 
    Create a layered layout where a semi-transparent overlay covers an image
    using z-index. Provide the HTML and CSS code snippets.

# Answer 08 : 
    We can create a layered layout by placing an overlay on top of an image using position and z-index.
    The image will be placed at the bottom layer, and the overlay will appear above it with some transparency.

    HTML Code
        <div class="container">
            <img src="image.jpg" alt="Sample Image">
            <div class="overlay">Overlay Text</div>
        </div>

    CSS Code :

        .container {
            position: relative;
            width: 300px;
        }

        .container img {
            width: 100%;
            display: block;
        }

        .overlay {
            position: absolute;
            top: 0;
            left: 0;
            width: 100%;
            height: 100%;
            background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5);
            color: white;
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            justify-content: center;
            z-index: 1;
        }

